eading Washington and Lee Receives Grant from the Teagle Foundation The planning grant will create a shared first-year humanities experience and expand pathways through the curriculum. Continue Reading Meet a Colleague: Rob Straughan Rob Straughan is the Crawford Family Dean of the Williams School of Commerce, Economics, and Politics. Continue Reading Get to Know the Newest Members of the W&L Community – 8/28/26 The following individuals recently joined the Washington and Lee employee workforce. Continue Reading Meet a Colleague: Colleen Drake Colleen Drake serves as senior program coordinator in the Division of Student Affairs. Continue Reading Washington and Lee Welcomes New Tenure Stream Faculty Twelve faculty members will join new positions during the 2026-27 academic year. Continue Reading W&L Announces New Fixed-Term Faculty, Fellows and Assistant Coaches Twenty-eight new faculty and staff members are joining the university this year. Continue Reading Convocation to Kick Off New Academic Year at Washington and Lee The event will be held at 5:30 p.m. Sept. 2 on the Front Lawn with remarks by Interim President Kenneth P. Ruscio ’76. Continue Reading Washington and Lee University Expands Tuition-Free Pledge to Families Earning up to $200K The expanded W&L Promise means new students entering W&L in fall 2027 whose families earn less than $200,000 will pay no tuition, and those whose families earn less than $75,000 will pay no tuition, room or board. Continue Reading Get to Know the Newest Members of the W&L Community – 8/19/26 The following individuals recently joined the Washington and Lee employee workforce. Continue Reading Dates and Deadlines University Calendar Sep 09 - 10:00 am - 4:30 pm Patrick Abelon with Creative Planning will be here on September 9, 2026 If you would like to make an appointment to meet with Patrick Abelon for personal financial planning through Creati Sep 09 - 1:00 pm - 3:30 pm Community Engagement Fair Come to the Community Engagement F