arroll from TIAA will be here on October 27, 2026 If you would like to schedule an appointment to meet with Rich Carroll regarding your TIAA retirement account, he w Oct 28 - 10:00 am - 4:30 pm Patrick Abelon with Creative Planning will be here on October 28, 2026 If you would like to make an appointment to meet with Patrick Abelon for personal financial planning through Creati Dec 02 - 10:00 am - 4:30 pm Patrick Abelon with Creative Planning will be here on December 2, 2026 If you would like to make an appointment to meet with Patrick Abelon for personal financial planning through SageVi Dec 03 - 10:00 am - 4:30 pm Patrick Abelon with Creative Planning will be here on December 3, 2026 If you would like to make an appointment to meet with Patrick Abelon for personal financial planning through Creati Events on Campus More from the Columns The Art Museum at Washington and Lee Presents ‘150 Years: A Collection Begins’ The exhibit, on view starting Sept. 2, celebrates 150 years of art stewardship at W&L. Continue Reading The Art Museum at W&L Presents ‘Zhang Xiaoli/Block Party!’ Opening Sept. 2, Zhang Xiaoli’s exhibit depicts imaginary worlds that blend traditional Chinese brushwork with playful, contemporary elements and pay homage to the enduring legacy of the late I-Hsiung Ju. Continue Reading W&L’s Staniar Gallery Presents Josh T Franco’s ‘FERAL (A History of Art)’ The solo exhibition opens Sept. 4 and kicks off the gallery’s fall season. Continue Reading W&L Community to Observe 25th Anniversary of the 9/11 Terrorist Attacks Washington and Lee will honor the lives lost on Sept. 11, 2001, with a series of commemorative events on campus Sept. 10 and 11. Continue Reading Campus Kitchen Announces 2026-2027 Just Food Series The annual event series examines how food systems interact with issues of social justice. Continue Reading W&L’s Lenfest Center Presents Screening of ‘BASQUIAT’ Jeffrey Wright stars as the visionary artist Jean-Michel Basquiat in the 1996 biopic. Continue Reading W&L to Host Constitution Day Panel on Supreme Court Cases from the 2025-26 Term The Liberating Ideas panel discussion takes place in Northen Auditorium on Sept. 16. Continue Reading W&L to Host ‘Meet the Press’ Panel with Virginia News Leaders Journalists from six news outlets in Virginia will discuss the current state of local journalism in a Sept. 16 panel moderated by W&L’s Eric Deggans. Continue Reading Maya Lin is the Next Speaker in the Mudd Lecture Series The architect and artist, who designed the Vietnam Veterans Memorial when she was 21, will give a lecture on Sept. 17 in Keller Theatre. Continue Reading The Art Museum at W&L Presents ‘The Legacy of I-Hsiung Ju’ Opening Sept. 18, the exhibit celebrates the work and legacy of the late professor of art emeritus and master Chinese brush painter I-Hsiung Ju. Continue Reading Employee Announcements Work Anniversaries Moves and Promotions In Memoriam This Week’s Work Anniversaries Recent Moves and Promotions In Memoriam Faculty and Staff Accomplishments Submit an Accolade Jill Fraley Publishes Article on Property, Sovereignty and Noncitizen Land Laws The article in the Indiana Law Journal Supplement examines the constitutional foundations of state laws restricting noncitizen ownership of real property. Continue Reading Opinio Juris Hosts Symposium on Mark Drumbl’s Reframing Transitional Justice Five scholars examine and respond to the new volume co-edited by Drumbl and Kirsten Fisher. Continue Reading Alex Rabar Profiled by the International Association of Campus Law Enforcement Administrators W&L’s chief public safety officer was featured in the member spotlight series “Behind the Uniform.” Continue Reading Bill Hamilton Interviewed on CBS Evening News Segment The John T. Perry Professor in Research Science discussed tourist-animal interactions following a recent bison attack in Yellowstone National Park. Continue Reading JT Torres Co-Authors Book Titled ‘Nonviolent Response’ Written with Sheri Rysdam of Eastern Oregon University, the book offers strategies for responding to writing in positive and motivating ways. Continue Reading Sociology Professor Receives Distinguished Dissertation Award Ivan Shmatko was cited by the Canadian Association for Graduate Studies after receiving a nearly perfect score from the program’s eight expert judges. Continue Reading Journalism Professor Headlines Discussion on First Amendment, Quoted in a Columbia Journalism Review article. Toni Locy was among three expert panelists to discuss the First Amendment at the National Press Club and was recently quoted on her professional experiences. Continue Reading Shannon Fyfe Publishes Article Challenging the Role of Genocide Law in Preventing Mass Atrocities New Loyola University Chicago Law Journal article argues that debates over whether violence constitutes genocide often distract from the need to end violence. Continue Reading Biology Faculty Member Co-Authors Paper in Global Ecology and Conservation Jacob Kraus and his research team studied a biodiverse area of China to determine the optimal sizes for nature reserves. Continue Reading Stephanie Sandberg Serves as a Guest Editor for the Critical Stages Journal The associate professor of theater worked with Nelson Barre of Roanoke College to introduce and assess four essays about modern theater. Continue Reading Lesley Wheeler’s Poem ‘Return Path’ is Featured on The Slowdown Podcast The poem is from the Henry S. Fox Professor of English’s 2025 book “Mycocosmic.” Continue Reading KT Vaughan Appointed to the Library of Virginia Board The Hal F. and Barbra Buckner Higginbotham University Librarian will serve a five-year term starting July 1, 2027. Continue Reading Browse or Create Campus Notices Read the latest announcements from around campus and/or create your own. Scene on Campus Scene on Campus is a frequently updated collection of candid photos highlighting W&L campus life. Browse the Archives of the Columns Weekly View Previous 